## Summary

`src/middleware.tsx` catches all errors from the rate-limiter call and allows the request to proceed as a fallback. If the Redis/Upstash service becomes unavailable, every subsequent request is allowed through with no throttling.

## Affected File

`src/middleware.tsx` (lines 30-34)

```typescript
try {
  // rate limit check
} catch (err) {
  console.error(err);
  // Fallback: allow request if rate limiter fails
}
```

## Impact

A targeted attack that exhausts Redis connections before hammering the AI endpoints completely bypasses rate limiting. The application has no fail-closed behavior for its primary abuse-prevention control.

## Suggested Fix

Change the catch block to return a 503 when the rate limiter is unavailable, rather than passing the request through:

```typescript
} catch (err) {
  console.error("Rate limiter unavailable:", err);
  return new Response("Service temporarily unavailable", { status: 503 });
}
```

## Severity

High

File: middleware.tsx
Description: The Next.js middleware is currently designed using a "fail-open" strategy. It defines an isProtectedRoute matcher that only explicitly protects /dashboard(.*), /profile(.*), and /admin(.*). It also defines an isPublicRoute matcher but never actually uses it in the logic. Because of this, any new page or API route added outside of those three folders is completely unprotected by default unless the developer remembers to manually add currentUser() checks inside the route. This is extremely prone to human error and leaves routes like /rooms unprotected at the middleware level.
Fix: Switch to a "fail-closed" (deny-by-default) model. You should check if the route is public, and if it's not, enforce authentication:
typescript


export default clerkMiddleware(async (auth, req) => {
    // ... rate limiting logic ...

    if (!isPublicRoute(req)) {
        const { userId, redirectToSignIn } = await auth();
        if (!userId) return redirectToSignIn();
    }
});

In the current UI, the text inside the "How It Works" and "Testimonials" sections is not clearly visible in light mode. The content appears too light, making it difficult to read

